If you know g0 (lambda0), sigma and sampling effort then I suspect there is nothing more to be learned from the spatial distribution of detections and you can put aside mark-resight etc. Can you clarify the nature of your unmarked detections - are they n distinct individuals or merely un-individuated cues? If the former then D-hat = n/a(g0,sigma) works just fine, given that a(g0,sigma) takes account of the spatial distribution and intensity of sampling effort. If we're talking about a certain number of cues C, rather than n, then possibly D-hat = C/E(C|D=1) using the function Enrm in secrdesign 2.5.2 to compute E(C) (see secrdesign-tools.pdf).  <http://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secrdesign-tools.pdf>
Murray

